    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Dublin base",
          "heading": "Jake White moves Fiji's captain's run from the Aviva to Kirwan Park",
          "body": "Jake White's Fiji have been training at De La Salle Palmerston FC, the junior club known locally as 'Salmo', and have felt so at home there that they decided to hold their captain's run on Friday at Kirwan Park rather than the Aviva Stadium. Non-playing squad members were due to train at the club again on Saturday morning. Club director of rugby Norman Byrne watched the sessions and said: \"They’re the nicest people you’ll ever come across.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Will Joseph equals try record",
          "body": "Italy fall 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's late error. France's Julien Marchand ruled out for rest of Nations Championship. Australia restore Carter Gordon to starting XV after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "The42"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Record haul",
          "heading": "Will Joseph's five tries match England record in 78-15 win over Japan",
          "body": "Will Joseph's second cap turned into a record-equalling afternoon as the wing crossed five times in England's 78-15 win over Japan on Saturday. Japan were a man down before they touched the ball, Harry Hockings sent off inside the first minute for a dangerous hit on Ellis Genge, and Joseph had a hat-trick inside 20 minutes. Five tries matches the England record held jointly by Douglas Lambert, Rory Underwood, Josh Lewsey and Henry Arundell, and England's 78 points were their biggest total for a quarter of a century."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Italy fall 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's late error",
          "body": "France's Julien Marchand ruled out for rest of Nations Championship. Australia restore Carter Gordon to starting XV after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Julien Marchand ruled out for rest of Nations Championship; Jalibert nears return",
          "body": "Planet Rugby understands that Julien Marchand has been ruled out for the rest of the Nations Championship. The hooker felt further thigh tightness in the warm-up before the South Africa win and had to pull out of the starting side, with Peato Mauvaka taking his place and Guillaume Cramont now the reserve hooker. The news is partly offset at fly-half, where Matthieu Jalibert, out since a quadriceps injury on 20 September, is expected at Marcoussis early next week and in line for the squad to face Argentina."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Will Joseph equals try record",
          "body": "Italy fall 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's late error. Australia restore Carter Gordon to starting XV after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury recall",
          "heading": "Ryan Baird recalls playing on with broken leg against South Africa",
          "body": "Ireland's Ryan Baird played on after a blow to the leg against South Africa at the Aviva Stadium in November 2025, convinced it was a dead leg. He went down, was strapped up, and only an X-ray in the stadium revealed a broken left leg. Tadhg Beirne, by Baird's account, told him to come off if he could not run. A comeback through two URC games and a Heineken Cup quarter-final was then interrupted by a second problem, and Baird says the year was soul-sapping."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Will Joseph equals try record",
          "body": "Italy fall 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's late error. France's Julien Marchand ruled out for rest of Nations Championship. Australia restore Carter Gordon to starting XV after broken leg."
        }
      ]
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Genoa defeat",
          "heading": "Italy fall 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's late missed touch kick",
          "body": "Italy's Genoa test against Argentina ended 19-14 to the Pumas on Saturday, and the last-minute error was Paolo Garbisi's. Trying to set up a lineout in a scoring position, the flyhalf missed a penalty touch kick, with the Azzurri having spent the closing stages pressing against 14 men after Efraín Elías was yellow-carded. Monty Ioane's early try and a second-half penalty try gave Italy their points. The Pumas won the game with three tries, and Italy remain winless in the competition."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Will Joseph equals try record",
          "body": "France's Julien Marchand ruled out for rest of Nations Championship. Australia restore Carter Gordon to starting XV after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Stadio Luigi Ferraris, Genoa"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Americas Rugby News"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Matchday honour",
          "heading": "Five-year-old Joey Sharp to deliver Murrayfield match ball for Scotland v Australia",
          "body": "Scottish Rugby have arranged for the five-year-old from Midlothian and his mother, Sam Sharp, to meet the Scotland players. Joey was diagnosed with a brain tumour at 11 days old and has had three surgeries and nine rounds of chemo, and he lives with cerebral palsy as a result of his treatment. He will deliver the ball alongside Commonwealth Games swimmer Archie Goodburn, and his mother says he is \"buzzing\" to meet the team. It will be his first game at Murrayfield, and his mother is a season-ticket holder."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Will Joseph equals try record",
          "body": "Italy fall 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's late error. France's Julien Marchand ruled out for rest of Nations Championship. Australia restore Carter Gordon to starting XV after broken leg."
        }
      ],
