      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Away trip",
          "heading": "Pumas travel to Paris after a difficult year of five defeats",
          "body": "Argentina go to Paris carrying a hard calendar year, and Rugbyrama's preview, written before Saturday's Genoa win, counts only one victory before it, against Wales. France are, in the paper's words, heavily depleted, but they have dominated the head-to-head: they won 37-23 when the teams last met in November 2024. Argentina's last win over France came in 2014, a game in which Nicolás Sánchez landed four drop goals."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Will Joseph equals try record",
          "body": "Italy fall 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's late error. France's Julien Marchand ruled out for rest of Nations Championship. Australia restore Carter Gordon to starting XV after broken leg."
