    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Les Kiss recalls Carter Gordon and Rob Valetini, drops Declan Meredith",
          "body": "Carter Gordon is back from the broken leg that has been the latest of several injuries to derail his progress, and Les Kiss has restored him to the starting XV for Sunday's Test against Scotland. \"Certainly Carter was the incumbent, so he was in a position of strength before he got injured,\" Kiss said. Rob Valetini is back in the starting side at six, while Declan Meredith, who looked lost in the defeat by England, has been dropped from match-day 23."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Will Joseph equals try record",
